1
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,119
I cut my arm. Look at it.

2
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,119
- It's not healing.
- Do you mean...?

3
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,639
I'm staying hurt.

4
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,399
Don't you see?
The whole world becomes immortal.

5
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:36,359
And I'm mortal. I don't mend.
I'm normal again.

6
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,719
This, Captain, fascinates me.

7
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:44,039
- What makes you so different?
- I don't know.

8
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:47,879
And yet you're the only one left,
the only true human. So tell me,

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,119
what did you give them so long ago?

10
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,719
Why would he want you dead?

11
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:56,359
On the very day that no-one's dying?
Wish I knew.

12
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:59,279
Every time you turn up,
it always go wrong.

13
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,999
Where are you from?

14
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,679
Long ago and so far away.

15
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,639
(HUBBUB)

16
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,639
MAN: Harkness. Anyone?

17
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,599
Jack Harkness.

18
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:21,039
I'm looking forJack Harkness.

19
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,719
That's me.

20
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,959
Welcome to America, Mr Harkness.

21
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,839
There's your visa all stamped.

22
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,999
Grazie. I mean,
thank you very much, Inspector.

23
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,919
Hey, wait! Stop that man!

24
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:45,359
(WHISTLES PEEP)

25
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,599
Come on now.

26
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,399
You're not Jack Harkness.
The visa's mine.

27
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,759
It's what?

28
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,599
You'll find everything's in order.

29
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,559
The British consulate arranged for my
travel through the embassy in Rome.

30
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,039
That visa belongs to me.

31
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:02,959
Yes, sir.
Terribly sorry this happened, sir.

32
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,919
Take him away. Send him back home.

33
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,279
- There you are.
- Thank you.

34
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:29,079
You're still here.
I thought you'd be in the city by now.

35
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,999
Time to spare.

36
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,919
Waiting for the next boat to Manhattan.

37
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:36,079
I also am waiting for a boat.
Mine goes all the way

38
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,839
- back to Italy.
- Right.

39
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:40,039
That's what they do with thieves.

40
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:48,679
An interesting fact is they do it
also with people who forge visas.

41
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,279
Good eye.

42
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,439
- Why didn't you tell them?
- I wasn't sure.

43
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:04,279
Until that moment when you said,
"Why didn't you tell them?"

44
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,599
(CHUCKLES)

45
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:08,799
I'm on a kind of unofficial
official visit,

46
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,879
one part of the government
pretending to be another part.

47
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,479
You work for a government?

48
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,999
Look at me.
Do I look like a bureaucrat?

49
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,319
Never seen a man like you before.

50
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,119
More like a soldier.

51
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,839
Your English is good. Where did you learn?

52
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,599
We had a schoolmaster in the village.

53
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,639
He taught me.

54
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:37,199
I went to him every single day
because I always dreamt of coming here.

55
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,319
- What's the village?
- You wouldn't know it.

56
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,999
No-one ever does.

57
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,759
Tiny place on the Amalfi Coast.

58
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:46,239
And I mean, for certain,
right on the coast.

59
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:50,199
The whole place is holding its breath
on the edge of a cliff top.

60
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:53,359
If you look over,
hundreds of feet down to the sea.

61
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:56,639
Sounds beautiful. Why'd you ever leave?

62
00:03:56,760 --> 00:04:01,079
New York. They have buildings here
taller than the cliff.

63
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,479
- I wanted to see that.
- You wait.

64
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,879
They've only just started building.

65
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,599
Years to come, they're going to have...

66
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:11,639
- What? They're going to have what?
- Never mind. What's your name?

67
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:17,559
Angelo Colasanto.

68
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,639
- La magia oscura!
- It's not magic.

69
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:30,079
Technology.
Sometimes they're indistinguishable.

70
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,479
Hey, hey, hey!

71
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,999
How does it work? Can I see it?

72
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,479
Hey, over here!

73
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,599
We just found this man's papers.

74
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,159
You can let him go.

75
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,399
We're going to Manhattan.

76
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,159
Who are you?

77
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,839
What do you want?

78
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,719
What do you want?!

79
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,279
(PHONE RINGS)

80
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,359
Rhys, call me, OK?

81
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,839
Mam, if you can, call me, OK?

82
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:01,999
Vera! Vera! Vera!

83
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,639
How many views have we got now?

84
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,919
Um, over five million.

85
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,199
People are setting up
memorial services for her too.

86
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:19,679
Just random people
who didn't even know her.

87
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,159
I just, um...

88
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,399
You got the footage

89
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,279
and that's going to make the difference.

90
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,279
But I've been meaning to say, I...

91
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,759
I know that that must have been...

92
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,999
I'm sorry.

93
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,039
I got ya.

94
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:39,599
No, really, Rex.

95
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,919
I really didn't even know her
that well, OK?

96
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,919
- But you did. You must have talked.
- Look, she...

97
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,919
she told me about her mother,
her ex-husband,

98
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,599
possibly something about
a brother or a sister.

99
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,679
I don't know, maybe not.

100
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,679
- The obituary says...
- Yeah. But what does it matter?

101
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:59,999
Hmm? Whoever she was, it's gone.

102
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:03,199
- I don't even know where she's from.
- The news is saying San Antonio.

103
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,439
Well, then, go Spurs!

104
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,679
Sorry.

105
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,559
I don't know how to help.

106
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:15,519
Except that...maybe her death
has changed things.

107
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,679
They'll shut down the camps.

108
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:22,159
No, they "paused" the camps.
That's all they're saying. Paused.

109
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:24,999
And while the politicians
are all denying everything,

110
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,959
those ovens are still out there,
waiting to burn.

111
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,159
- (DOOR OPENS)
- Jack!

112
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,159
- Gwen, you're back.
- Where's Jack?

113
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,439
Sorry about your dad.

114
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,079
- Did you hear any news?
- No, not really.

115
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,759
- Jack!
- He went outside.

116
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,599
- Jack?
- Hey!

117
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,279
I missed you.

118
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,479
I've been searching
through that Blessing stuff.

119
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,519
Listen, you've got to come down to
the car. I've got to show you something.

120
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:48,239
- Anything good?
- No, just stuff from back home.

121
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,439
Souvenir sort of thing.
Just you and me. Come on.

122
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:53,199
All right, stop your nagging.
Told you she missed me(!)

123
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,079
GWEN: Yeah, today would be good, Jack.

124
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,159
- (DOOR CLOSES)
- Bad day, Gwen?

125
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:04,159
Ohh!

126
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,239
(CAR HORN BLARES)

127
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,199
All right. OK.

128
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:18,359
(SHE SPEAKS ITALIAN)

129
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,079
I'm sorry. My Italian isn't so...

130
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:43,839
She's saying there is only one bed.

131
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,279
- (SPEAKS ITALIAN)
- Ah!

132
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,199
- I said I'll sleep on the floor.
- On the floor, yes.

133
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,879
(SHOUTING) He'll sleep on the floor.

134
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,239
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

135
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,079
Come-a down to the shop any time.

136
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:03,039
Family butcher's is fine food.

137
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,399
And you are family now.

138
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,039
It's a good room.

139
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,959
And it's cheap.

140
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,359
You should save your money,
Angelo Colasanto.

141
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,599
Next couple of years,
earn as much as you can.

142
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,559
Save it all up

143
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,959
cos you're going to need it.
Bad times ahead.

144
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,879
Why, what's going to happen?

145
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,839
Oh! Oh, so many things.

146
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:41,239
Don't worry. It gets better.

147
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,479
Then it gets worse again.

148
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,119
You talk funny.

149
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,719
I'm a very funny man.

150
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,239
Scars.

151
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,999
You been in a lot of fights?

152
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:01,799
Sometimes you have to defend yourself,
you know?

153
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:06,000
People...say things.

154
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,079
(TYRES SQUEAL)

155
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,319
RADIO: Another non-stop hour
of music, weather...

156
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,839
(SWITCHES STATION)

157
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,719
...and allegations continue to surface

158
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:20,199
about procedures
at the new medical facilities.

159
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:23,399
But Oswald Danes has released
a statement in which he says

160
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,239
that a global emergency
calls for emergency measures

161
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,719
and he advocated a swift return
to the category policy.

162
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,359
Ah! I'm tied down.

163
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,199
- Why am I tied down?
- They're in my eyes.

164
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:37,199
- What?
- They're in my eyes.

165
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,359
The contacts. They're in my eyes.

166
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:41,039
Somebody's taken Anwen, Rhys,
my mother, the whole bloody family,

167
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:42,959
and they've said if I bring you,
they'll let them go unharmed.

168
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,599
Don't try moving.
You'll never get out of those knots.

169
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:50,599
My... My hands are asleep.

170
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,319
And my feet. You tied my feet?!

171
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,519
Of course I did, stupid.
Otherwise you'd get out of the car,

172
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,839
knock me out and turn the car around.

173
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:01,799
- Are you sure they have your family?
- I phoned 1 00 times.

174
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:05,319
There's no reply.
They... They've got them.

175
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:08,519
I want to talk to the lenses.
Look at me so I can talk to them.

176
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,119
Why do you always keep thinking
you can tell me what to do?

177
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:15,079
Pull over or look into the rear-view.
Just, please, let me talk to them.

178
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,199
Don't cock this up, OK?

179
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:24,319
Listen, whoever you are,
there's more than one way to play this.

180
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,679
Are you listening?

181
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,559
Yeah, there's a cursor. They're there.

182
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,399
You want me?

183
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,799
Let her family go
and I'll come to you alone.

184
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,759
- Tell them they can have me too.
- No, just me.

185
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:41,199
Let Rhys go, let Anwen go,
let her mother go free.

186
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:44,879
You guys, you know what?
Here I am. You got me.

187
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,839
GWEN: Nothing.

188
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,399
- Give them a minute.
- There's just nothing now.

189
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,799
- Maybe they're thinking about it.
- My mother's name is Mary.

190
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,079
Mary!

191
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,599
You've known me all this time
and you can't remember her name?

192
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,719
- All right, I'm sorry, OK?
- Yeah. Well, you should be,

193
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,919
because this is all your fault.

194
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:00,959
They want to kill you,
but why do they want to do that?

195
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,519
- I don't know.
- What have you done?

196
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,639
I don't know!

197
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:06,359
Well, you've done something,
haven't you?

198
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,199
Way back when
in that long bloody life of yours.

199
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,719
God, you've lived so long, you can't
remember half of it. Now you think.

200
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,479
Think! What the hell have you done?

201
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,079
JACK: I love this. I love weddings.

202
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,559
I don't believe in marriage.

203
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,799
So young, so handsome and so cynical.

204
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:27,719
ANGELO: Look at them.

205
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,719
What are their chances?

206
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:33,839
That's what makes it
so brave and wonderful...

207
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:35,119
making a promise and going forward.

208
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:37,839
It doesn't matter
what happens in the future.

209
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:41,399
Right now, it's real
and it happens and it's true.

210
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,559
You're Catholic, right?

211
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:49,479
Do you want to kneel down like that?

212
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,759
He doesn't hear me.

213
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,399
He doesn't hear you? Why?

214
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,879
You know why.

215
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:02,999
That's our padre. Wait here.

216
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:09,639
Forgive me, Father, for I have sinned...
so many times,

217
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,719
and that's just today.

218
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:18,679
It's been about...700 years
since my last confession.

219
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,279
Where do I start?

220
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,799
How about the triplets?

221
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:26,599
Or the naked circus?

222
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:29,759
Or that Sapphic leapfrog jamboree?

223
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,519
(CHUCKLES)

224
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:35,319
(CLEARS THROAT) No.

225
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:41,999
Let's just start with the sin of...
"Father Timothy sent me."

226
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,999
(LATCH CLICKS)

227
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,999
- You're Jack Harkness?
- Good to see you, Father.

228
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,719
I believe we're going to talk business.

229
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:55,359
The Volstead Act makes an exception
for sacramental wines.

230
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:58,199
And the brothers upstate
produce more than we can use.

231
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:02,399
The extra income feeds
a lot of widows and orphans, I'm sure.

232
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:06,959
Yes, I'm doing this entirely
for charity, every last cent.

233
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,559
It's not very good.

234
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:11,239
It's the blood of Christ, Angelo.
I'm sure it's good enough.

235
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,919
This is just a sample.

236
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,759
If you make enough profit,
we'll start delivering crates.

237
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,999
We should figure out a system.

238
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:21,199
Hey, what are you doing?
Who are you?

239
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,279
It's OK.
Let them take us, Angelo. It's OK.

240
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,799
Where are they taking us?

241
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,879
I don't know where. Just east.

242
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,879
Did they say get on the 1 0 going east?

243
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,119
Or on the eastbound 1 0 Freeway,
or what?

244
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:38,039
If they said highway,
they could be from back east.

245
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:39,559
If their grammar was wrong,

246
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,119
it could mean that English
is not their first language.

247
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,159
- I didn't notice anything wrong with it.
- You're Welsh.

248
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,359
You wouldn't notice
if the vowels were missing.

249
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:45,719
Button it!

250
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,639
Hey, you've got a gun, haven't you?

251
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,439
- You could smuggle it back here to me.
- It's gone.

252
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,679
They made me leave it behind.

253
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,079
Just give it up, Jack,
with all this planning, OK?

254
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,559
Because if there was a way out of this,

255
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,999
I can guarantee you
I would have thought of it.

256
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:08,119
Gwen, I shouldn't... There are reasons
I shouldn't even say this...

257
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,879
secrets...

258
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,839
but we could...we could find Anwen.

259
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,879
My wrist strap, it could find her.

260
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,119
We could save her.

261
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,719
What?

262
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:22,039
It's coded to my DNA.

263
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:24,839
And it resonates
to anything close to my DNA.

264
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,039
If you are using my daughter
as leverage, I swear to God,

265
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,559
- I will kill you myself.
- Listen to me.

266
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:32,599
If we recode it to your DNA,
then Anwen is a close match.

267
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,439
It would respond to her.
Like a tracker.

268
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:39,119
We could save her together.
We could rescue her.

269
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,719
You could do that?
You could do that recode thing?

270
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:46,479
Yes. A drop of your blood. A single cell
would do, but a drop would be easier.

271
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,599
- Let's do it.
- Pull over.

272
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,199
OK, let's do it. I'll have to untie you.

273
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,879
One hand forjust a second,
all right, Gwen?

274
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:55,439
I'd be saving Anwen.

275
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,279
You bastard.

276
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,559
Nice try.

277
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,879
GWEN: Oh, mm-hmm.

278
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,559
Whoever this is...they know you.

279
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,359
Phew!

280
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:29,999
So, Mr Harkness...and his acolyte.

281
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,319
- Yeah, and who are you?
- Your friend thinks he's funny.

282
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:35,679
He doesn't. He isn't. He's sorry.
This is Sal Maranzano.

283
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,319
- You were going to undercut my price.
- We found some untapped resource.

284
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,199
Rumour is you two are a pair of finocchi.

285
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,279
That's not a rumour. That's a boast.

286
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:49,359
And if you were really upset about
some small-time competition,

287
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,119
it'd already be hailing bullets.

288
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,919
So we're here for another reason.

289
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:55,919
I don't think so. Take 'em, kill 'em.

290
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,519
Give us a try, Maranzano.

291
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:00,799
You need men like us, off the grid.

292
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,879
Men who could never
be traced back to you.

293
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,079
So whatever it is you need, Sal,
no matter how dangerous it is,

294
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,759
no matter how strange it is,

295
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:10,159
you just found the right men.

296
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,679
There's a box in a warehouse

297
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:18,359
that needs to find its way
to another warehouse.

298
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,999
You can count on us.

299
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,599
You will not look in the box.

300
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,999
Sure thing.

301
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:32,519
You will swear...
on everything that is holy

302
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:36,599
you will deliver the box,
but you will not look inside.

303
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,999
I promise.

304
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,719
Then we got a deal.

305
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,759
Tomorrow night, Gallaco Wharf, Bay Five.

306
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,999
Get going. Get lost.

307
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:03,039
- You're running away?
- No.

308
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,239
That's mine! Wh...

309
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,279
What are you doing?

310
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,719
You're packing my things!

311
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:12,159
You need to go now. There's a plan.

312
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,479
And I'm not part of your plan?

313
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:15,959
Look at your hands. Not a scar on them.

314
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,839
I'm tougher than you.

315
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:21,199
Maranzano's people
have stumbled across something

316
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:24,079
they're not supposed to have.
I've got to stop them.

317
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,439
You made this happen?

318
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,199
You've planned this.

319
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:33,359
Since when?
Since you got on the boat to America?

320
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,839
Just get out of town, Angelo.
These people are bad.

321
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,159
You don't want to be on their list.

322
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,999
- Get far away.
- Who are you doing this for?

323
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:43,239
The government in England?
Or the other thing you said...Torchwood?

324
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,879
For the train. Go to the West Coast.

325
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,199
You're handsome enough.
Get into the movies.

326
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:49,079
- I'm not letting you send me away.
- Why?

327
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,639
Because you wouldn't know
how to get another man?

328
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,239
Because you're not brave enough?

329
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,879
You think I'm with you because it's easy?

330
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,119
- It's not easy, trust me.
- I know.

331
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,999
I hear the beads clicking
at night, Angelo.

332
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:02,359
Everything we do,
you ask for forgiveness afterwards.

333
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,599
That's just sex. Imagine if it was love.

334
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:08,159
What would he say then, your God?
What would he say if two men could love?

335
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:11,359
Oh! Oh, but no. No, that's impossible.

336
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:14,359
And if it's impossible,
then you can't stay with me.

337
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,479
You...

338
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:17,599
...you're an ass.

339
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,639
For a man who knows a lot of things,
huh, you're not so bright.

340
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,239
Think about it.

341
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:26,159
I grew up in a village with 200 people.

342
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,559
Only 200.

343
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:31,679
The sun would rise and the sun would set
over the same 200 people.

344
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:35,399
And that was it. That was my world.

345
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,039
And look at me now.

346
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:42,399
I'm a bootlegger in New York City
with you in my bed.

347
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,959
You think any of your little secrets

348
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:47,039
can change my life
more than it's already changed?

349
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,999
And yes, I...

350
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:51,399
I feel guilty about what we do.

351
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:54,879
It hasn't made me stop doing it.

352
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:18,599
Besides, I always hoped...

353
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:22,719
...if God is love,

354
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,959
maybe...

355
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,319
he loves me too.

356
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:28,039
That's blasphemy.

357
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,079
I think that's Christianity.

358
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,719
You're unpacking my things?

359
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,079
I've got this friend.

360
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,079
He's called The Doctor.

361
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:02,639
He explores the world...

362
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,079
...with a companion.

363
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,199
It looks nice.

364
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:16,559
Are you saying that I can stay?

365
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:20,159
Maybe.

366
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:49,479
Oh, Dio.

367
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,319
What's all this?

368
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,919
Ammonia refrigeration. Of course!

369
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:56,039
The best they could do in 1 927.

370
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,239
They said, "Don't look in the box."

371
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:01,799
- Yeah, right(!)
- What is it? What's inside?

372
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,079
Someone...

373
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:07,039
Someone way above Maranzano,
they found something, a weapon.

374
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:09,759
They told Maranzano to hold it

375
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:12,039
until after the next state election,
then ship it to Albany.

376
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:15,719
Maranzano doesn't know what he's got,
but he's terrified of it.

377
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:21,039
Can't say I blame him.

378
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:23,959
No. No, that's...

379
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,199
What?

380
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:29,959
Er, it's a parasite. Like a bug.

381
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:31,879
A parasite?

382
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,359
Tell me more about it.

383
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:36,999
Good man.

384
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,199
It's a species of brainspawn

385
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:43,119
treated as vermin on more than
1 50 planets that I know of.

386
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:45,959
And valued as dinner on one other.

387
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:48,759
It tastes like oysters.

388
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:51,559
- You did not.
- I had to be polite.

389
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:56,639
Now this part drills
into the brain of the host

390
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:59,159
and deposits its larvae there...

391
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,199
little worms,

392
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:05,599
sharp as needles,
pushing into the brain very slowly.

393
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:08,799
You go insane, but it takes years.

394
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:10,399
Franklin Roosevelt,

395
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:13,639
he's going to be elected governor
of New York this November.

396
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,199
But he wouldn't start making
the really crazy decisions

397
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,079
until his second term as president.

398
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:23,239
Result - America destabilises,
pulls out of the war, Germany rises,

399
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:27,599
the Third Reich triumphant, and there's
a whole new history sprawling out.

400
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:29,639
You mean someone is changing the future?

401
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,439
Destroying it.

402
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:34,519
Turning order into chaos
and feeding off the results.

403
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:38,279
Who would do such a thing?
These people above Maranzano.

404
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:41,959
They're just being used by someone
called The Trickster's Brigade.

405
00:23:42,080 --> 00:23:44,439
Believe me, you don't wanna meet them.

406
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:46,319
What sort of men are they?

407
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,799
They're not men at all.

408
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,719
They're not even human.

409
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:54,279
OK. OK.

410
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:57,759
Ah, he likes you.

411
00:23:57,880 --> 00:24:00,399
But it's cold, yeah? So it's safe?

412
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:01,719
- (HISSING)
- Oh, Dio!

413
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:05,799
Ha!

414
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,999
That'll dissolve it.

415
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,079
Ah!

416
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:16,199
So...the mission is complete.

417
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,879
We just saved the world, Angelo.

418
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:22,319
- And no-one will ever know.
- Then, did I pass?

419
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:25,119
Can I stay with you like The Doctor?

420
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,879
Learn all the secrets?

421
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,679
- (ALARM BELL RINGS)
- Here's one of the secrets...

422
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:29,839
run!

423
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,119
Quick. Come on, up. Let's go!

424
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:45,359
Hold it! Stop right there!

425
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:47,119
Take my hand.

426
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:48,279
Ah!

427
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,679
- Grab my hand!
- (CAPTAIN JACK PANTS)

428
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,199
- (GUNSHOT)
- No!

429
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,799
(DOG BARKS)

430
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,239
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

431
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:11,719
(THEY SHOUT OVER EACH OTHER)

432
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,439
All right, get him in there.

433
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:27,079
Go! Get him up the stairs. Step up.

434
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,439
Jack.

435
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:33,719
Meat cart's on the way for the other one.

436
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:36,359
You'd better take the main gate.
Off you go.

437
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:39,559
(SIREN WAILS)

438
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:48,439
(GASPS)

439
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,879
It's me.

440
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,519
- What do you mean?
- Well, it's me.

441
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,759
I caused this.

442
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:18,999
I made this...happen.

443
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:22,799
I knew Torchwood was toxic...

444
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:26,439
right from the moment I joined up,
the very first day, but...

445
00:26:26,560 --> 00:26:28,039
I stayed.

446
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:34,079
- I'm glad you did.
- Hah! Stop being so nice.

447
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:37,879
We left nice behind 1 00 miles back.

448
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,319
I'm trying to be honest, OK?

449
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:42,919
Because do you know what
the worst thing is of all?

450
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:46,279
Out of all the shit we have seen,
all the bloodshed,

451
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:49,919
all the horror, do you know
what is worse than all of that?

452
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:54,039
I loved it.

453
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:01,199
I bloody loved it.

454
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:04,359
And I'd keep telling Rhys I was sorry

455
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:08,239
and I'd say to little Anwen, "I'm sorry,"
but I loved it so much.

456
00:27:10,280 --> 00:27:14,439
I knew things no-one else knew
and, oh, I felt so special.

457
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:19,919
And when we lost people,
it was so, so big

458
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:24,799
and I could say it was worth it,
because the bigger it was,

459
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,679
the more important I was.

460
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:28,039
And the more people we lost...

461
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:32,119
...the more that meant I was a survivor
and I was better than them.

462
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,239
My God, this is all my fault.

463
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:34,999
And now they've got
my beautiful little girl

464
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:37,319
and I've wished this on her.

465
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,799
I used to think the same
about Torchwood...

466
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:42,079
That's what I'm saying.
Have you got what I'm saying to you, Jack?

467
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:44,519
What I'm saying is, no more.

468
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:48,279
Cos I know exactly what you're thinking,
Jack Harkness. I know it.

469
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:49,799
"She won't do this.

470
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,639
"Not really. Not my Gwen.

471
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:53,439
"No, Gwen, she can't hurt me.

472
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:56,119
"Gwen loves me.
She'd never hand me in."

473
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,959
Well, this is about my daughter.

474
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:02,799
And I swear, for her sake,
I will see you killed like a dog

475
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:06,519
right in front of me if it means
her back in my arms. Understood?

476
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:07,679
Understood.

477
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:11,679
And let me tell you,

478
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:14,119
now that I'm mortal,

479
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:16,319
I'm going to hang on to this
with everything I've got.

480
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:20,279
I love you, Gwen Cooper,
but I will rip your skin from your skull

481
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:22,879
before I let you take this away from me.

482
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:24,679
Understood?

483
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:26,159
Understood.

484
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:37,239
I feel like I know you now
better than I've ever done before.

485
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,119
Yeah.

486
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:45,959
- Right at the end.
- Mmm.

487
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:49,279
Right at the end.

488
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,559
Nice suit.

489
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:05,879
Look, it's all right. Don't panic.

490
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:09,839
- It's me. I'm the same man.
- I saw you.

491
00:29:09,960 --> 00:29:11,399
I saw you get shot.

492
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:14,599
- I got better.
- You got shot in the head.

493
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:18,119
I saw it. I saw the blood, I...

494
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,439
I saw your body.

495
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:23,999
- Want to see it again?
- Shut up, Jack!

496
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:29,039
This is so wrong.

497
00:29:33,360 --> 00:29:36,159
Tell me...what happened.

498
00:29:38,560 --> 00:29:39,639
You were dead.

499
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:41,439
Clearly, I wasn't.

500
00:29:42,520 --> 00:29:43,559
I was playing dead.

501
00:29:44,920 --> 00:29:45,839
Then I cleared out.

502
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:49,599
- I went to Los Angeles.
- No, I saw you dead.

503
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:51,399
But I'm alive.

504
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:55,839
Feel.

505
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:58,159
You wanted to learn the secrets?

506
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:02,079
This is the best secret of all.

507
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,999
You're alive.

508
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:09,679
I'm alive.

509
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:14,959
I came back, Angelo.

510
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:18,599
I came back for you. Believe me,
I have never done that before.

511
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:21,799
I... I even got us that same old room.

512
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:25,239
You came back for me?

513
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:27,799
Yes. Yes, I did.

514
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:32,519
You don't know whether to hit me
or to kiss me, do you?

515
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:34,439
Come on,

516
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:36,319
you can try both.

517
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:42,039
(DOG BARKS, SIRENS WAIL)

518
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:48,719
What the hell, Angelo?

519
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,319
What did you do?

520
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:53,119
Il diavolo!

521
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,919
I am not the devil.

522
00:30:55,040 --> 00:30:58,359
It's the only way.
The devil seduces with confidence.

523
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:01,959
No. No!

524
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:07,199
- Stay away from me, devil!
- Ah!

525
00:31:07,320 --> 00:31:09,359
Ah! God!

526
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:32,639
(HE GASPS, SHE SCREAMS)

527
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:35,719
- Il diavolo! Il diavolo!
- Jack...

528
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:37,279
Il diavolo!

529
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,519
Ah!

530
00:31:42,760 --> 00:31:45,839
I don't understand. Angelo,
I don't understand. What did he do?

531
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:48,199
- We can show you.
- É un miracolo.

532
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:49,519
A miracle?

533
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:54,119
I want to see. Do it again.

534
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:57,759
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

535
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:05,159
JACK: No.

536
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:07,399
No.

537
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:21,799
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

538
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:24,239
(GASPS)

539
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:26,559
- (CROWD GASPS)
- Diavolo!

540
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:29,159
Angelo...

541
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:30,719
Angelo!

542
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:33,519
Don't go!

543
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:51,039
(JACK SCREAMS)

544
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:56,999
MAN: I don't know.

545
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:01,079
I just don't know what it is.

546
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:04,719
Hmm. How much is the butcher asking?

547
00:33:04,840 --> 00:33:10,319
1 0,000. Not too much for something
with so much potential.

548
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:13,279
And we'd own him...together?

549
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:17,559
A partnership. What do you say?

550
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:28,199
Agreed.

551
00:33:42,080 --> 00:33:43,239
This is it.

552
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:46,439
It's been a long time coming.

553
00:33:48,080 --> 00:33:49,679
All those years.

554
00:33:50,960 --> 00:33:54,239
What's the most beautiful thing
you've ever seen? Not just on Earth.

555
00:33:54,360 --> 00:33:56,919
I'm not doing this,
I'm not giving final speeches.

556
00:33:57,040 --> 00:33:58,719
Just tell me,
anywhere in the universe.

557
00:34:05,720 --> 00:34:07,159
I saw a firebird once,

558
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:08,959
a tiny little thing,

559
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,439
even smaller than a hummingbird.

560
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:13,639
- Oh?
- Literally made of fire.

561
00:34:16,160 --> 00:34:17,519
It only lives for a minute.

562
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:21,599
It blazes different colours...and sings.

563
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:26,879
It gets so bright
you have to close your eyes.

564
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:30,519
And when you open them, it's gone.

565
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:38,199
But the image stays behind your eyelids
for longer than it was alive.

566
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:40,439
Tell me another one.

567
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:42,599
- I've said enough.
- No, go on, tell me.

568
00:34:42,720 --> 00:34:44,039
Just tell me about your life,

569
00:34:44,160 --> 00:34:46,559
all the things that you've never said.

570
00:34:46,680 --> 00:34:48,679
How many children did you have, Jack?

571
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:51,319
I've lived a lot of lifetimes, Gwen,
I can't tell you everything.

572
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:54,439
A lot of lifetimes.
That's a consolation, isn't it? Is it?

573
00:34:54,560 --> 00:34:56,319
When you've had
more lives than anyone...

574
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,199
It's not enough.

575
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,999
- I don't want to die.
- I know.

576
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:08,919
I'm so sorry, Jack.

577
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:10,559
It just...

578
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:14,679
It went crazy, like...like bloodlust.

579
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:15,799
I was so scared.

580
00:35:15,920 --> 00:35:18,399
Are you going to take the wrist strap?

581
00:35:19,680 --> 00:35:21,879
I'm a good thief.
I could have taken it any night.

582
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,599
You'd better clean up.

583
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:27,479
We've got to go. Can you stand?

584
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:28,959
Give me a minute.

585
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:42,039
I bought some inattention from Nico,

586
00:35:42,160 --> 00:35:44,279
the guy who's supposed to be
watching you,

587
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:46,159
but it won't last for ever.

588
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:47,679
You can put these on.

589
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:50,919
Who were the three men?

590
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:53,599
What men?

591
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:55,119
There were three men.

592
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:58,599
Like they were making...

593
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:00,479
an agreement.

594
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:02,879
I don't know. Hurry up.

595
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:13,479
ANGELO: Hurry,
there's a train out tonight!

596
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:15,359
Train where? Where are we going?

597
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:18,359
Like you said, we'll go to the West Coast,
Los Angeles, together.

598
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:29,359
Jack!

599
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:33,039
Where are you going?

600
00:36:33,160 --> 00:36:34,799
I left something here.

601
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:39,479
You left something in a vent on a roof?

602
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:43,319
Ha! Never go far without it.

603
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:53,799
- OK, but now we go.
- I'm going, yeah.

604
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,079
Time to move on.

605
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:58,639
But not with you.

606
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:04,479
I'm sorry.

607
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:09,679
I was terrified, Jack.
They said you were the devil,

608
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:10,959
but other people said
you were a blessing...

609
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:12,719
Something happened to me once,

610
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:14,759
a long way away.

611
00:37:14,880 --> 00:37:20,559
Time itself changed me
to a...fixed point. And now I can't die.

612
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:23,439
I suffer and I perish...

613
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,479
...but I always come back.

614
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:31,279
I've lived through a lot of Earth's past
and a lot of its future.

615
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,959
And I'll keep on
living this life for ever.

616
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:36,439
- In the future, are we together?
- What does it matter?

617
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:37,639
- Are we together?
- We can't be,

618
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:39,599
cos one day you're going to die

619
00:37:39,720 --> 00:37:41,519
- and I won't.
- Then we forget the future.

620
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:44,239
We make the moment now.

621
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:47,319
- We make a promise and we go forward.
- Angelo,

622
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:50,039
- don't.
- What? You're lonely, too.

623
00:37:50,160 --> 00:37:51,439
You said you want a companion.

624
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:53,359
- Don't make me do this.
- You're not going without me!

625
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:55,559
- Just let me go.
- But you can't!

626
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:56,919
I'm never going to let you go.

627
00:37:57,040 --> 00:37:59,439
I could travel this whole wide world,

628
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:01,959
but where would I find
another man like you?

629
00:38:02,080 --> 00:38:05,999
Please, don't leave me on my own.

630
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,679
I'm sorry, Angelo,

631
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:14,239
but this is the story of my life.

632
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:17,479
It always ends the same way.

633
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:21,919
You kill me.

634
00:38:30,440 --> 00:38:31,879
Men like you...

635
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:36,839
- ...you kill me.
- No!

636
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:45,039
No! No!

637
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:47,959
No! Jack!

638
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,599
- Know her?
- No.

639
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:26,959
- OK.
- WOMAN: Thank you.

640
00:39:27,080 --> 00:39:31,319
You followed the instructions,
as far as I can tell.

641
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:32,919
Captain Harkness,

642
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:34,839
the last mortal man.

643
00:39:36,160 --> 00:39:38,159
It has been a long journey.

644
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:44,799
- (GUNSHOT)
- What the hell?!

645
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:46,239
- Find out who that is!
- It's on you.

646
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:48,239
Who is it?

647
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:49,519
What the hell are they doing?!

648
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:52,639
(GUN COCKS)

649
00:39:52,760 --> 00:39:54,239
Gotcha.

650
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:56,079
Bad day, Gwen?

651
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:57,799
(BEEPING)

652
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:15,079
- Rex.
- Yeah?

653
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:17,359
Rex, you gotta see this.

654
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:20,079
I was just checking the cache
on the I-5s. Look what it says.

655
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:23,319
- Can we track them?
- Yes.

656
00:40:23,440 --> 00:40:24,799
Oh, Gwen!

657
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:27,759
- You ready?
- I'm ready.

658
00:40:27,880 --> 00:40:29,639
Must be Rex and Esther.

659
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:31,639
- She's still got Anwen.
- Not for long.

660
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:35,239
Uh, you've got a little something
on you there.

661
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:39,199
Now unless you want to be
diagnosed Category 1 ...

662
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:41,519
Put your guns down.

663
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:46,439
OK, get back! Get back! Back!

664
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,799
- Her hands are up.
- Yes.

665
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:54,039
Go, go, go!

666
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:58,199
- All right, go, go, go!
- (THEY SHOUT ORDERS)

667
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:01,239
Grid one! Check him out!

668
00:41:01,360 --> 00:41:03,559
One down. Living room clear.
Spread out, follow the grid.

669
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:04,959
Yes, sir. Jackson, with me.

670
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:08,759
Rhys, I can't believe it. We got you,
don't worry. You're all right.

671
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:10,479
Took your bloody time!

672
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:12,479
Yes, I know, Mrs Cooper.
It's been frantic.

673
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:13,719
We got this call. I was off duty...

674
00:41:13,840 --> 00:41:15,439
Gun, gun, gun!

675
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,839
I've never shot anyone before.

676
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:23,919
Where's Gwen?

677
00:41:24,040 --> 00:41:27,639
Andy! What's happened to Gwen?

678
00:41:34,240 --> 00:41:36,199
It's OK. It's OK.
Your family and baby, they're safe.

679
00:41:37,280 --> 00:41:40,199
Next time, just ask for help. I'm sick
of Torchwood acting like amateur clowns.

680
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:42,079
Oh, you did it! Thank you!

681
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:43,639
Got it?

682
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:45,599
Thank you.
And you, you're going to live.

683
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:46,879
It's a talent of mine.

684
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:47,919
I meant every word I said.

685
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:48,999
- So did I.
- Good.

686
00:41:49,120 --> 00:41:50,559
And as for you...

687
00:41:50,680 --> 00:41:52,319
you'd better pray
that death comes back to this planet

688
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,439
by the time I'm finished with you.

689
00:41:53,560 --> 00:41:56,159
So tell us who you are,
before I let her loose.

690
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:59,759
I don't see that anything's changed.

691
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:01,319
You're still coming with me.

692
00:42:01,440 --> 00:42:03,719
- Why would I do that?
- You'll want to come with me

693
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:07,799
because I can take you to the one man
who knows how the miracle began.

694
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,919
- Who's that?
- Angelo.

695
00:42:10,040 --> 00:42:12,959
Angelo Colasanto.

696
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:14,959
He's waiting for you, Jack.

697
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:20,679
He's been waiting
for such a very long time.

698
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,319
They don't exist.

699
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:32,519
- Shit!
- What is it, Rex?

700
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:34,519
Everybody, stay where you are!
Back down.

701
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:36,399
OK, OK, all right.

702
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:41,279
- Leave me alone with him.
- (GRUNTS)

703
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,479
- Goddamn it!
- Shit.

704
00:42:48,600 --> 00:42:50,839
While you were wasting time, Mr Shapiro,

705
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:52,279
we've got the names of the people
who are responsible

706
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:55,519
for causing the miracle.
I suggest we get to work.

707
00:42:55,640 --> 00:42:58,279
He's preaching hellfire and salvation,
which makes Oswald Danes

708
00:42:58,400 --> 00:42:59,919
the most popular man in the world
right now.

709
00:43:01,040 --> 00:43:02,599
Get me a girl.

710
00:43:02,720 --> 00:43:04,839
How old?

711
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:06,519
Mr Danes?

712
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:10,079
I can act all kinds of innocent.

713
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,119
Don't presume to know me.

714
00:43:11,240 --> 00:43:14,399
I am capable of far more
than my...reputation.

715
00:43:14,520 --> 00:43:16,159
(GIGGLES)

716
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:18,759
I said...don't presume.

717
00:43:20,120 --> 00:43:23,759
Actually, if you don't mind,
I think I'd like to go.

718
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:25,959
Don't! Don't you dare!

719
00:43:27,520 --> 00:43:29,999
This is like the whole world
is changing...

720
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:32,959
...and we're just so tiny.

721
00:43:33,080 --> 00:43:34,959
There's a reason why Torchwood was secret.

722
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:36,879
We kept things hidden from the human race.

723
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:41,879
This technology is a science
the world should never know.

724
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:43,919
This thing would be the end of us.
